# E230 diagnostic — v3 patch (corrected after grok-cli1 measured defects)
#
# v2 had three patch defects and three gate defects. v3 fixes the three
# patch defects:
#
#   (5) THRESHOLD: v2 used 9 * capacity (37,748,736), nine TIMES the
#       ceiling, not 90% of it. v3 hardcodes 3,774,873 = floor(
#       4194304 * 9 / 10) into the runtime check, and the relationship
#       is documented in the comment block above the threshold load.
#       If the capacity constant in gc.sio is ever changed, this
#       threshold must change in lockstep.
#
#   (6) ITOA ASSIGNMENT: emit_inline_itoa_stderr is pass-by-value and
#       returns NativeCompiler; v2 dropped the result at four call sites
#       (two in the failure diagnostic, two in the 90% warning fire body).
#       v3 captures the result with `nc = emit_inline_itoa_stderr(nc)`
#       at every site. The drop was a silent-defect class: the function
#       ran, but the new cursor state was never propagated to the rest
#       of the emitter, leaving any code emitted after an itoa call
#       working from a stale NativeCompiler. Confirmed by the same
#       inspection that says `c = emit_inline_itoa_stderr(c)` is the
#       only call pattern in the file today.
#
#   (structural boundary) v3 captures the WHOLE OLD function in hunk 2's
#       OLD block (including the closing `}` and the trailing syscall
#       sequence). v2's hunk 2 inserted the new helpers + new function
#       between `let write_len = ...` and `let lea_pos = ...`, which
#       left the OLD syscall tail orphaned inside the new function
#       and produced a parse-broken `fn ... fn ... }` nested
#       definition. v3 fixes that with a 1-for-1 function replacement.
#
# Two new helpers are introduced:
#       nc_write_rodata_to_stderr_into and nc_append_rodata_bytes
#       factor the sys_write emission and the byte-array rodata
#       appends. Both are pure emitters — they take nc by `&!`
#       reference so the caller never has the assignment problem the
#       patched call sites do.
#
# Gate defects fixed in a SEPARATE atomic commit on the gate:
#   (1) W2/W3 now run the produced ELF with timeout and check stderr.
#   (2) Witness structs use 3 i64 fields (tag = 24) so the struct exceeds
#       the unbox threshold (gc.sio: native_v2_is_small_value_struct_tag
#       returns false for tag > 16). Each alloc therefore consumes a handle.
#   (3) W1 dropped: Layer-1 compile-time refusal is a defence-in-depth path
#       not yet present in the checker (defect 4), and the generated
#       source file would exceed the 16 MB / 2048 locals IR ceiling. W2/W3
#       cover the dynamic-count failure family that d2_gum belongs to.
#       W1 is moved to docs/audit/HANDLE_TABLE_CEILING_REFUSAL_REFINEMENT_2026-08-17.md
#       as the design-layer description of the path that will land when
#       the checker grows the E230 arm.
#
# Build lane application notes:
